		(uuid "0a175489-2386-487a-ab50-a51b9db631a6")
	)
	(text "Emitter follower into the ADC: more light = higher.\nLoad: 10k to start; 4k7-100k so the open beam\nreads ~2/3 of full scale with its slits in."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 210.82 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "38ebda61-d747-48bd-b355-9a49dba6d1b6")
	)
	(text "PHOTOTRANSISTORS (PT1206BS)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 210.82 119.38 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4080a681-53ee-4a02-a94f-959c52745173")
	)
	(text "Two slots in an L, on the bed outside the paper area (it moves with the bed). Each slot 15 mm long,\nan IR LED at one end, a PT1206BS at the other (on its side: it is top-view), each behind a slit.\nX beam: along Y, crossed by moving in X. Y beam: along X, crossed in Y. The pen does the L.\nSlits: two razor-blade edges, 0.2-0.3 mm apart, narrow across the pen's travel. Beam 1-2 mm over the bed:\ncrossed 0.5-1.5 mm over the tip (its z from the load cell). Measure Y first, then cross X at every\npen's same spot along the beam (a beam off square reads X off by its angle). Notes: limn/TODO.md, break-beam."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 198.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "40b2a730-5de8-4b98-aaee-6494b6951323")
	)
	(text "BEAM BED: XY by two IR break-beams (Z: the head's load cell)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5326b5bf-e0ef-4a86-9c9e-b5099d4969d5")
	)
	(text "The bed ID: a free one of BED_1..6\n(the Dock's bands end at 33k): to pick."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 142.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "59c0e8fe-e8b7-4e4d-9ec1-f3dfedf45e1f")
	)
	(text "GP0: BED_DATA, a half-duplex UART on one wire (PIO).\nGP1: BED_PROBE, high = OK; low when armed and the beam's\nedge is seen. On the plot bed board it is in series with\nthe touch line (Q952): Klipper's probe pin, no relay in\nfirmware. DETECT: the ID resistor only.\nGP28/29 (ADC2/3): free, for a second pair later."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 91.44 99.06 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5d799597-7b06-428b-8b33-bb720b6287c9")
	)
	(text "Beam node (under the beam block)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 92.71 24.13 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "883b2473-5a47-430b-b328-fa4fb6f082da")
	)
	(text "AO3400: logic level, the 100k holds it off through a reset.\n~35 mA pulsed from BED_PWR (5 V): (5 - 1.3) / 100R.\nOn minus off at a few kHz cancels room light.\nX and Y on their own pins: only one lit at a time,\nso the X LED can't leak into the Y phototransistor."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 210.82 101.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d0fa3706-5c32-44f3-8d38-5dbc0b6847e8")
	)
